      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test file contains:\n1. A large number of unused data provider methods (only `data_samples` is used by the actual test)\n2. All sample pairs on a single very long line making `data_samples()` nearly unreadable\n3. A large number of unused imports\n\nI'll produce an improved version: remove unused data providers, clean up imports, and format `data_samples()` for readability.Now let me compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused data provider methods and imports, reformats `data_samples()` with one entry per line (with inline comments explaining leap-year, St. Tib's Day, and century-year cases), and adds short Javadoc on both the class and the test method to make the intent immediately clear."
